FreeImage
---------

Copyright the FreeImage project contributors
(https://freeimage.sourceforge.net).

FreeImage is bundled as a shared library (`libFreeImage.dylib` / `.so` / `.dll`)
and gives OCCT its image codecs: without it, reading an image file fails on
every platform but Windows and writing produces a PPM under whatever extension
is asked for. FreeImage is used under the FreeImage Public License version 1.0
(FIPL), rather than its alternative GPL licensing options:

    licenses/FreeImage-FIPL.txt

The FIPL is an MPL-1.1 derivative. Its sections 3.6 and 3.7 permit distributing
the executable form inside a larger work under a licence of our choice, provided
the licence text travels with it and this notice says where the source is.
**nanocct does not modify FreeImage.** Its complete corresponding source is the
tag pinned in `deps/fetch-freeimage-src.sh` (3.19.15) at
https://github.com/danoli3/FreeImage.

FreeImage vendors the codecs it uses, so the following are compiled into that
one library. It is built with BUILD_WEBP, BUILD_OPENEXR, BUILD_LIBRAWLITE and
BUILD_JXR off, so libwebp, the OpenEXR codec, LibRaw (the only CDDL component)
and jxrlib are **not** included; JBIG-KIT is not vendored by FreeImage at all.

    zlib                    licenses/zlib.txt
    libpng                  licenses/libpng.txt
    libjpeg (IJG)           licenses/libjpeg-IJG.txt
    libtiff                 licenses/libtiff.txt
    OpenJPEG (BSD-2)        licenses/OpenJPEG-BSD-2-Clause.txt
    Imath "Half" (BSD-3)    licenses/Imath-Half-BSD-3-Clause.txt

The OpenEXR image codec is disabled and no separate OpenEXR library is bundled.
The OpenEXR-derived half-float implementation (Source/OpenEXR/Half/half.cpp,
which FreeImage builds unconditionally for its 16-bit float pixel type) is
compiled into FreeImage.

The build is configured to keep the bundled codec implementations private and
expose FreeImage's public API.


